# Node.js (m4tr!x)

Use only when captain approved a **custom backend** (not pure Firebase client).

- Clear module boundaries; validate inputs at the edge
- Structured errors; no silent catch-and-ignore
- Secrets via env — never commit `.env` with real credentials
- Tests for critical paths; document run/deploy in `docs/sdlc/DEPLOYMENT.md` when relevant
- Prefer TypeScript when starting greenfield Node services unless captain says otherwise

If the only JS/TS is Flutter tooling or unrelated scripts, do not force a Node service architecture.
